# Assumption Registry

Spec: Assumptions
Purpose:
  Define the Assumption object — explicit, tracked assumptions that AI
  makes when planning and executing. Assumptions are NOT decisions; they
  are unverified beliefs that must be validated. When invalidated, triggers
  replanning of dependent tasks.

Owns: assumptions/

## Assumption Object Schema

  @assumption.A12

  assumption:
      provider refund API is synchronous

  confidence:
      low

  used_by:
      @task.T102

  status:
      PROPOSED

  created:
      2026-09-01

## Assumption Lifecycle

  PROPOSED → VALIDATED → RESOLVED
  PROPOSED → INVALIDATED → REPLAN_TRIGGERED

## Assumption Risk Levels

  LOW       — minimal impact if wrong
  MEDIUM    — moderate impact, needs eventual validation
  HIGH      — significant impact, validation required before critical task
  CRITICAL  — must be validated before ANY execution

## Rules

  [ASM-01] Assumption ≠ Decision. Assumptions are unverified; decisions are evidence-based.
  [ASM-02] Every assumption MUST track confidence level (low/medium/high/critical).
  [ASM-03] Every assumption MUST track which tasks/requirements it affects.
  [ASM-04] When assumption is invalidated, dependent tasks MUST trigger replan.
  [ASM-05] AI MUST surface unresolved assumptions before executing HIGH/CRITICAL risk tasks.
  [ASM-06] Assumptions are NOT silently resolved — status MUST be explicitly updated.

  Example:
    A12: provider refund API is synchronous
    confidence: low
    used_by: T102 (Provider integration)

    → If A12 is invalidated (API is actually async):
      T102 → BLOCKED
      T103 → BLOCKED (depends on T102)
      AI proposes T102b (Webhook handler)
      Plan replanned with T102a, T102b

